        "content": "# 🛠️ Setup Guide  \n**Author:** [Nate Herk](https://www.youtube.com/@nateherk)\n\nFollow the steps below to get this workflow up and running:\n\n### ✅ Step 1: Connect Fireflies to Your Webhook  \nIn your [Fireflies](https://fireflies.ai/) settings, configure your webhook URL to point to the n8n webhook trigger in this workflow. This is what kicks off the automation after each meeting.\n\n### ✅ Step 2: Add Your Fireflies API Key  \nGet your API key from [Fireflies](https://fireflies.ai/) and connect it to all Fireflies nodes in the workflow.\n\n### ✅ Step 3: Copy the Google Sheet  \n[Make a copy of this Google Sheet](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/u/1/d/1Stc1guUXnYIYoxTZwznv3EMRQ-esZmR5RFuhoVbsffw/copy) to your own Google account. This is where your meeting data will be logged. Then connect your Google credentials to the Google Sheets node.\n\n### ✅ Step 4: Connect Your Slack Credentials  \nLink your Slack workspace so the workflow can send you messages asking whether you'd like a proposal generated.\n\n### ✅ Step 5: Add Your OpenRouter API Key  \nConnect your [OpenRouter](https://openrouter.ai/) credential to power the AI agent that generates your proposals.\n\n### ✅ Step 6: Create Your Gamma API Key  \nGenerate an API key from [Gamma](https://gamma.app/) and add it to the HTTP Request node for Gamma. This enables automatic proposal creation.\n\n### 💡 How It Works  \nOnce everything is connected, your next Fireflies meeting will automatically be logged in the Google Sheet. You'll then receive a Slack message asking if you want a proposal generated — just respond and let the AI do the rest!",
